Vikram and Betal: The Careful Listener (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100131

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a young boy who liked to talk a lot,” said Betal. “He never listened to others.”

One day, his teacher gave instructions for an important task.

But the boy did not listen carefully.

He made many mistakes.

Another boy listened quietly and followed every instruction.

He completed the task perfectly.

The teacher praised the second boy.

The first boy felt sad and asked, “Why did I fail?”

The teacher said, “Because you spoke more and listened less.”

The boy understood his mistake and decided to change.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, what is the lesson here?”

Vikram replied, “Listening carefully is just as important as speaking.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Good listening leads to success.
